    {
      "id": "b648558c-7dbd-57dc-a14e-b10b5faa9cdb",
      "title": "School podcast on growing up and making a difference",
      "titleEn": "School podcast on growing up and making a difference",
      "description": "Die lernende Person kann eine materialgestützte E-Phasen-Aufgabe zu Jugendperspektiven, Kommentierung und Mediation im Fach Englisch bearbeiten.",
      "descriptionEn": "The learner can solve a material-based E-phase task on youth perspectives, commentary, and mediation in English.",
      "weight": 1,
      "tags": [
        "GK",
        "LK",
        "Practice",
        "Assessment"
      ],
      "contains": [],
      "requires": [
        "544aad84-4c32-4e31-9a32-6bfa1310ff72",
        "de8e479b-55cc-40dd-8ba6-2143fb65135a",
        "a294c6a3-7f40-43c2-af27-2d5d76537e2c"
      ],
      "dimensionTags": {
        "framework": "hessen-kc-2024-english",
        "demandLevel": "AB3",
        "processCompetencies": [],
        "guidingIdeas": [],
        "phase": "E"
      },
      "examData": {
        "taskContent": "**Context:**\n\nYour school is planning an English-language podcast episode on *growing up and making a difference*.\n\n**Material 1:** a short blog post by a teenager about pressure at school.  \n**Material 2:** a short report on a youth volunteering project.  \n**Material 3:** an infographic with survey data on social media and well-being.\n\n**Tasks:**\n\n1. Summarise the central message of material 1 and identify two stylistic features. (5 pts)\n2. Explain how material 2 presents young people as agents of change. (5 pts)\n3. Use material 3 to compare two trends and comment on their relevance for teenagers. (5 pts)\n4. Write a short podcast introduction in English that connects all three materials for your audience. (5 pts)",
        "solutionContent": "1. A coherent summary and two justified stylistic observations are expected.  \n   **5 pts**\n\n2. The explanation should identify perspective, examples and intended effect.  \n   **5 pts**\n\n3. The comparison should use the infographic correctly and comment on relevance.  \n   **5 pts**\n\n4. The podcast introduction should be audience-aware, coherent and linguistically appropriate.  \n   **5 pts**",
        "scoring": {
          "maxPoints": 20,
          "passingPoints": 12,
          "steps": [
            {
              "id": "s1",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Blog post summarised and style identified accurately"
            },
            {
              "id": "s2",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Role of young people explained convincingly"
            },
            {
              "id": "s3",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Survey data compared and commented on correctly"
            },
            {
              "id": "s4",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Podcast introduction written appropriately for audience"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "phase": "E"
    },
    {
      "id": "224b4c9d-55e8-52df-b029-75950bb719b3",
      "title": "Civic responsibility between student debt and self-optimization",
      "titleEn": "Civic responsibility between student debt and self-optimization",
      "description": "Die lernende Person kann eine materialgestützte Q1-Aufgabe zu sozialer Verantwortung, Leistungsdruck und politischer Teilhabe im englischsprachigen Raum bearbeiten.",
      "descriptionEn": "The learner can solve a material-based Q1 task on social responsibility, performance pressure and civic participation in the English-speaking world.",
      "weight": 1,
      "tags": [
        "GK",
        "LK",
        "Practice",
        "Assessment"
      ],
      "contains": [],
      "requires": [
        "b460e077-d42b-48df-a56a-d20edd560f86",
        "c0833654-e44b-4594-90db-239ac5575a23",
        "39639b5a-12a8-47ad-889b-a5d02b726ab3"
      ],
      "dimensionTags": {
        "framework": "hessen-kc-2024-english",
        "demandLevel": "AB3",
        "processCompetencies": [],
        "guidingIdeas": [],
        "phase": "Q1"
      },
      "examData": {
        "taskContent": "**Context:**\n\nYou are preparing a school debate on whether young adults can still combine personal ambition with civic responsibility.\n\n**Material 1:** feature extract about a first-generation college student balancing part-time jobs, volunteer work and academic expectations.  \n**Material 2:** short opinion text arguing that self-optimization culture weakens solidarity.  \n**Material 3:** chart on student debt, unpaid internships and youth participation in local initiatives.\n\n**Tasks:**\n\n1. Analyse how material 1 presents pressure, ambition and responsibility. (5 pts)\n2. Explain the central argument in material 2 on individual success and solidarity. (5 pts)\n3. Compare the position in material 2 with the data in material 3. (5 pts)\n4. Write a reasoned comment on whether competitive success today leaves enough room for civic engagement. (5 pts)",
        "solutionContent": "1. The analysis should identify the pressures on the student, the balancing of ambitions and obligations, and the overall tone.  \n   **5 pts**\n\n2. The explanation should state the central claim about self-optimization and solidarity clearly.  \n   **5 pts**\n\n3. The comparison should connect the normative position to the data in a plausible and differentiated way.  \n   **5 pts**\n\n4. The comment should be balanced, material-based and coherent, leading to a clear judgement on civic engagement under competitive conditions.  \n   **5 pts**",
        "scoring": {
          "maxPoints": 20,
          "passingPoints": 12,
          "steps": [
            {
              "id": "s1",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Pressure, ambition and responsibility analysed coherently"
            },
            {
              "id": "s2",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Central argument on success and solidarity explained accurately"
            },
            {
              "id": "s3",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Opinion text and data compared convincingly"
            },
            {
              "id": "s4",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Comment on civic engagement argued in a coherent and material-based way"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "phase": "Q1"
    },
    {
      "id": "959a6a98-48d5-5cf4-b2c2-5c48bbe55c00",
      "title": "Individualism, social diversity and gender expectations on campus",
      "titleEn": "Individualism, social diversity and gender expectations on campus",
      "description": "Die lernende Person kann eine materialgestützte Q1-Aufgabe zu Individualismus, Diversität und Genderrollen im englischsprachigen Raum bearbeiten.",
      "descriptionEn": "The learner can solve a material-based Q1 task on individualism, diversity and gender roles in the English-speaking world.",
      "weight": 1,
      "tags": [
        "GK",
        "LK",
        "Practice",
        "Assessment"
      ],
      "contains": [],
      "requires": [
        "c0833654-e44b-4594-90db-239ac5575a23",
        "39639b5a-12a8-47ad-889b-a5d02b726ab3",
        "fd068ac5-d0f3-45ed-be53-c5628a66e145"
      ],
      "dimensionTags": {
        "framework": "hessen-kc-2024-english",
        "demandLevel": "AB3",
        "processCompetencies": [],
        "guidingIdeas": [],
        "phase": "Q1"
      },
      "examData": {
        "taskContent": "**Context:**\n\nAn international school newspaper is collecting student opinions on freedom, belonging and gender expectations.\n\n**Material 1:** opinion piece on conformity vs. individualism at college.  \n**Material 2:** short interview extract on gender expectations.  \n**Material 3:** cartoon on diversity and social stereotypes.\n\n**Tasks:**\n\n1. Analyse the line of argument in material 1. (5 pts)\n2. Explain how material 2 presents gender expectations and identity. (5 pts)\n3. Interpret the cartoon in material 3 in the context of social diversity. (5 pts)\n4. Write an editorial paragraph on how schools can support individuality without ignoring social responsibility. (5 pts)",
        "solutionContent": "1. A structured analysis of thesis, arguments and language is expected.  \n   **5 pts**\n\n2. The explanation should identify relevant aspects of gender and identity.  \n   **5 pts**\n\n3. The interpretation should connect visual and thematic elements meaningfully.  \n   **5 pts**\n\n4. The editorial paragraph should argue clearly and use the material productively.  \n   **5 pts**",
        "scoring": {
          "maxPoints": 20,
          "passingPoints": 12,
          "steps": [
            {
              "id": "s1",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Argumentative structure analysed"
            },
            {
              "id": "s2",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Gender and identity issues explained"
            },
            {
              "id": "s3",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Cartoon interpreted in context"
            },
            {
              "id": "s4",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Editorial paragraph argued coherently"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "phase": "Q1"
    },
    {
      "id": "d6b5343f-d007-5168-8ef5-1463744b9fe9",
      "title": "Britain after Brexit: identity, tradition and change",
      "titleEn": "Britain after Brexit: identity, tradition and change",
      "description": "Die lernende Person kann eine materialgestützte Q2-Aufgabe zu Großbritannien, nationaler Identität und Wandel bearbeiten.",
      "descriptionEn": "The learner can solve a material-based Q2 task on Great Britain, national identity and change.",
      "weight": 1,
      "tags": [
