      ],
      "dimensionTags": {
        "framework": "hessen-kc-2024-english",
        "demandLevel": "AB3",
        "processCompetencies": [],
        "guidingIdeas": [],
        "phase": "Q2"
      },
      "examData": {
        "taskContent": "**Context:**\n\nYou are preparing background material for an exchange project on contemporary Britain.\n\n**Material 1:** newspaper feature on Brexit and regional divisions.  \n**Material 2:** short speech on British identity and stereotypes.  \n**Material 3:** map-based infographic on migration and population change.\n\n**Tasks:**\n\n1. Analyse how material 1 presents tradition and change. (5 pts)\n2. Explain the concept of British identity in material 2. (5 pts)\n3. Use material 3 to comment on migration-related change in the UK. (5 pts)\n4. Write a balanced summary for German exchange students on what currently shapes the character of the nation. (5 pts)",
        "solutionContent": "1. The analysis should identify perspective, examples and evaluative language.  \n   **5 pts**\n\n2. The explanation should discuss identity, stereotypes and self-perception.  \n   **5 pts**\n\n3. The commentary should use the infographic correctly and meaningfully.  \n   **5 pts**\n\n4. The summary should be balanced, audience-aware and coherent.  \n   **5 pts**",
        "scoring": {
          "maxPoints": 20,
          "passingPoints": 12,
          "steps": [
            {
              "id": "s1",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Tradition and change analysed"
            },
            {
              "id": "s2",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "British identity explained"
            },
            {
              "id": "s3",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Migration data commented on correctly"
            },
            {
              "id": "s4",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Audience-oriented summary written"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "phase": "Q2"
    },
    {
      "id": "1a42e1c7-bd8e-5d89-b28f-aacd3eed9ca1",
      "title": "Tourism, housing and Indigenous perspectives in New Zealand",
      "titleEn": "Tourism, housing and Indigenous perspectives in New Zealand",
      "description": "Die lernende Person kann eine materialgestützte Q2-Aufgabe zu Tourismus, Wohnraumdruck und indigenen Perspektiven in Neuseeland bearbeiten.",
      "descriptionEn": "The learner can solve a material-based Q2 task on tourism, housing pressure, and Indigenous perspectives in New Zealand.",
      "weight": 1,
      "tags": [
        "GK",
        "LK",
        "Practice",
        "Assessment"
      ],
      "contains": [],
      "requires": [
        "11079440-96ce-4946-b6c2-2a9a4cd32414",
        "1859cab6-9994-408f-b1b6-83e420d634fe"
      ],
      "dimensionTags": {
        "framework": "hessen-kc-2024-english",
        "demandLevel": "AB3",
        "processCompetencies": [],
        "guidingIdeas": [],
        "phase": "Q2"
      },
      "examData": {
        "taskContent": "**Context:**\n\nA youth forum is discussing whether international tourism still benefits local communities in New Zealand.\n\n**Material 1:** article on tourism growth, short-term rentals and housing pressure in a New Zealand region.  \n**Material 2:** commentary by a Māori voice on land, belonging and community interests.  \n**Material 3:** infographic on visitor numbers, rents and conservation funding.\n\n**Tasks:**\n\n1. Summarise the central argument of material 1. (5 pts)\n2. Analyse how material 2 evaluates the relationship between economic benefit, land and community. (5 pts)\n3. Explain what material 3 suggests about tourism-related change. (5 pts)\n4. Write a position statement on how tourism, local housing and cultural responsibility should be balanced. (5 pts)",
        "solutionContent": "1. The summary should identify the key argument and relevant evidence on tourism and housing pressure.  \n   **5 pts**\n\n2. The analysis should discuss viewpoint, reasoning and evaluative language concerning land, community and responsibility.  \n   **5 pts**\n\n3. The explanation should interpret the infographic correctly and relate it to the broader debate.  \n   **5 pts**\n\n4. The position statement should balance economic opportunities, housing needs and cultural responsibility while remaining material-based.  \n   **5 pts**",
        "scoring": {
          "maxPoints": 20,
          "passingPoints": 12,
          "steps": [
            {
              "id": "s1",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Tourism and housing argument summarised"
            },
            {
              "id": "s2",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Indigenous perspective analysed"
            },
            {
              "id": "s3",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Tourism-related data interpreted"
            },
            {
              "id": "s4",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Position on tourism, housing and responsibility argued coherently"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "phase": "Q2"
    },
    {
      "id": "decfe395-472b-5c98-8403-7f5a6787992a",
      "title": "Deepfakes, visual evidence and public trust",
      "titleEn": "Deepfakes, visual evidence and public trust",
      "description": "Die lernende Person kann eine materialgestützte Q3-Aufgabe zu digitaler Bildmanipulation, Glaubwürdigkeit und öffentlichem Vertrauen bearbeiten.",
      "descriptionEn": "The learner can solve a material-based Q3 task on digital image manipulation, credibility and public trust.",
      "weight": 1,
      "tags": [
        "GK",
        "LK",
        "Practice",
        "Assessment"
      ],
      "contains": [],
      "requires": [
        "853240bb-5efc-4304-bcbf-b7a451566947",
        "60e7443b-0cda-405f-8360-c5e736b2adca"
      ],
      "dimensionTags": {
        "framework": "hessen-kc-2024-english",
        "demandLevel": "AB3",
        "processCompetencies": [],
        "guidingIdeas": [],
        "phase": "Q3"
      },
      "examData": {
        "taskContent": "**Context:**\n\nA media literacy workshop is discussing how deepfakes and manipulated images affect public trust.\n\n**Material 1:** short narrative extract about a teenager confronted with a convincing fake video.  \n**Material 2:** article on verification routines, fact-checking and visual evidence online.  \n**Material 3:** infographic on how manipulated content spreads before corrections reach the public.\n\n**Tasks:**\n\n1. Analyse how material 1 presents uncertainty and loss of trust. (5 pts)\n2. Explain the argument of material 2 on verification and credibility. (5 pts)\n3. Interpret material 3 in relation to the speed and impact of misinformation. (5 pts)\n4. Write a short review comment on whether societies can still rely on visual evidence in digital media environments. (5 pts)",
        "solutionContent": "1. A coherent analysis of perspective, uncertainty and trust is expected.  \n   **5 pts**\n\n2. The explanation should state key arguments on verification and credibility accurately.  \n   **5 pts**\n\n3. The interpretation should connect the infographic to circulation speed, correction delays and misinformation effects.  \n   **5 pts**\n\n4. The review comment should develop a balanced argument on visual evidence and public trust in digital media.  \n   **5 pts**",
        "scoring": {
          "maxPoints": 20,
          "passingPoints": 12,
          "steps": [
            {
              "id": "s1",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Uncertainty and trust analysed coherently"
            },
            {
              "id": "s2",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Argument on verification explained accurately"
            },
            {
              "id": "s3",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Infographic on misinformation interpreted meaningfully"
            },
            {
              "id": "s4",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Review comment on visual evidence developed convincingly"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "phase": "Q3"
    },
    {
      "id": "4c66c92d-8df9-5f7d-bd75-b1c4f3768390",
      "title": "Belonging, memory and conflicting narratives",
      "titleEn": "Belonging, memory and conflicting narratives",
      "description": "Die lernende Person kann eine materialgestützte Q3-Aufgabe zu Zugehörigkeit, Erinnerung und konkurrierenden Erzählungen bearbeiten.",
      "descriptionEn": "The learner can solve a material-based Q3 task on belonging, memory and conflicting narratives.",
      "weight": 1,
      "tags": [
        "GK",
        "LK",
        "Practice",
        "Assessment"
      ],
      "contains": [],
      "requires": [
        "fd068ac5-d0f3-45ed-be53-c5628a66e145",
        "81166ed9-85fb-4097-915a-51800f70a61a",
        "1859cab6-9994-408f-b1b6-83e420d634fe"
      ],
      "dimensionTags": {
        "framework": "hessen-kc-2024-english",
        "demandLevel": "AB3",
        "processCompetencies": [],
        "guidingIdeas": [],
        "phase": "Q3"
      },
      "examData": {
        "taskContent": "**Context:**\n\nA literature and society course explores how belonging is shaped by family memories, migration experiences and conflicting public narratives.\n\n**Material 1:** short-story extract about a teenager negotiating family expectations and social belonging.  \n**Material 2:** article on contested memories and identity debates in a multicultural society.  \n**Material 3:** quotation set on home, memory and belonging.\n\n**Tasks:**\n\n1. Analyse how material 1 presents inner conflict and belonging. (5 pts)\n2. Explain how material 2 links public memory and identity formation. (5 pts)\n3. Compare the ideas of belonging in materials 1 and 3. (5 pts)\n4. Write a reasoned statement on whether shared narratives help or hinder social cohesion. (5 pts)",
        "solutionContent": "1. The analysis should identify the inner conflict, perspective and the character's struggle for belonging.  \n   **5 pts**\n\n2. The explanation should discuss how collective memory shapes identity and public debate.  \n   **5 pts**\n\n3. The comparison should work out similarities and differences in the understanding of belonging precisely.  \n   **5 pts**\n\n4. The statement should develop a clear and well-supported argument on narratives and social cohesion.  \n   **5 pts**",
        "scoring": {
          "maxPoints": 20,
          "passingPoints": 12,
          "steps": [
            {
              "id": "s1",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Belonging conflict analysed precisely"
            },
            {
              "id": "s2",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Public memory and identity linkage explained clearly"
            },
            {
              "id": "s3",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Ideas of belonging compared accurately"
            },
            {
              "id": "s4",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Statement on social cohesion argued with good support"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "phase": "Q3"
    },
    {
      "id": "43291171-523d-5b11-bc59-de8bad628800",
      "title": "AI, sustainability and responsibility in science and technology",
      "titleEn": "AI, sustainability and responsibility in science and technology",
      "description": "Die lernende Person kann eine materialgestützte Q4-Aufgabe zu Wissenschaft, Technik, Nachhaltigkeit und Verantwortung bearbeiten.",
      "descriptionEn": "The learner can solve a material-based Q4 task on science, technology, sustainability and responsibility.",
      "weight": 1,
      "tags": [
        "GK",
        "LK",
        "Practice",
