        "guidingIdeas": [],
        "phase": "Q4"
      },
      "examData": {
        "taskContent": "**Context:**\n\nA local council is considering the use of AI-supported systems in urban energy management.\n\n**Material 1:** report on AI in public infrastructure.  \n**Material 2:** commentary on ecological costs of digital technologies.  \n**Material 3:** chart on energy savings in smart-city projects.\n\n**Tasks:**\n\n1. Summarise the main idea of material 1. (5 pts)\n2. Analyse the critical perspective in material 2. (5 pts)\n3. Explain what material 3 suggests about opportunities and limits. (5 pts)\n4. Write a recommendation for the council on how innovation and responsibility can be balanced. (5 pts)",
        "solutionContent": "1. The summary should identify the key idea and relevant context.  \n   **5 pts**\n\n2. The analysis should discuss stance, arguments and language.  \n   **5 pts**\n\n3. The explanation should interpret the chart plausibly.  \n   **5 pts**\n\n4. The recommendation should balance innovation, sustainability and responsibility.  \n   **5 pts**",
        "scoring": {
          "maxPoints": 20,
          "passingPoints": 12,
          "steps": [
            {
              "id": "s1",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Infrastructure report summarised clearly"
            },
            {
              "id": "s2",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Critical commentary analysed"
            },
            {
              "id": "s3",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Energy chart interpreted correctly"
            },
            {
              "id": "s4",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Recommendation balanced and coherent"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "phase": "Q4"
    },
