        "phase": "Abitur"
      },
      "examData": {
        "taskContent": "**Part 2 - Writing with integrated reading comprehension**\n\n**Material 1:** article on the idea of equality in American democracy.  \n**Material 2:** personal account by a second-generation immigrant student.  \n**Material 3:** cartoon on conformity and success.\n\n**Tasks:**\n\n1. Analyse how material 2 presents chances and obstacles in American society. (8 pts)\n2. Explain how material 1 frames democratic ideals and opportunity. (7 pts)\n3. Interpret the cartoon in material 3 in the context of conformity vs. individualism. (5 pts)\n4. Write a comment for an online debate on whether the American Dream is still a productive idea for a diverse society. (10 pts)",
        "solutionContent": "A strong solution analyses the migrant perspective in detail, explains the democratic ideals in the non-fiction text, interprets the cartoon meaningfully and develops a well-structured, material-based comment on the American Dream.  \n**30 pts**",
        "scoring": {
          "maxPoints": 30,
          "passingPoints": 18,
          "steps": [
            {
              "id": "s1",
              "points": 8,
              "description": "Chances and obstacles analysed in detail"
            },
            {
              "id": "s2",
              "points": 7,
              "description": "Democratic ideals explained accurately"
            },
            {
              "id": "s3",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Cartoon interpreted in context"
            },
            {
              "id": "s4",
              "points": 10,
              "description": "Comment argued coherently and material-based"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "phase": "Abitur"
    },
