        "phase": "Abitur"
      },
      "examData": {
        "taskContent": "**Part 2 - Writing with integrated reading comprehension**\n\n**Material 1:** essay on the promises and blind spots of American democracy.  \n**Material 2:** literary extract about migration, ambition and belonging.  \n**Material 3:** visual commentary on individualism, conformity and public expectation.\n\n**Tasks:**\n\n1. Analyse how material 2 presents identity formation under social pressure. (8 pts)\n2. Explain and evaluate the central claim in material 1. (7 pts)\n3. Interpret material 3 in relation to conformity vs. individualism. (5 pts)\n4. Write an argumentative essay on whether individualism strengthens or weakens democratic society in the USA. (10 pts)",
        "solutionContent": "A strong solution analyses identity formation in depth, explains and evaluates the essay's claim, interprets the visual commentary insightfully and develops a differentiated argumentative essay on individualism and democracy.  \n**30 pts**",
        "scoring": {
          "maxPoints": 30,
          "passingPoints": 18,
          "steps": [
            {
              "id": "s1",
              "points": 8,
              "description": "Identity formation analysed in depth"
            },
            {
              "id": "s2",
              "points": 7,
              "description": "Central claim explained and evaluated"
            },
            {
              "id": "s3",
              "points": 5,
              "description": "Visual commentary interpreted insightfully"
            },
            {
              "id": "s4",
              "points": 10,
              "description": "Argumentative essay differentiated and well-structured"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "phase": "Abitur"
    },
    {
